  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon Emergency Response for Displaced People in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Aleppo, Rural Damascus, Damascus, Deir ez -Zor, Homs, Hama, Dar&apos;a, Lattakia, and Idlib, support 25,000 individuals with the following: 1 - WASH: Emergency water trucking, Provision of water tanks and latrines, solarization/Quick fix/repair of WASH infrastructure in hosting sites or in community, Solid waste management,  support water testing and O&amp;M by local authorities, Hygiene awareness session with kits distribution 2 - Shelter: One -off emergency cash for rent or basic needs, distribution of winterization kits 3 - Protection: protection and gender analysis, IPA, provision of Protection/dignity items including kits for PLW 4 - MPCA for 3 months  Targeted Beneficiaries: Oxfam is aiming to reach a total of 5,000 HHs from hosting and displaced families. It is estimated to include 25,000 individuals (13,000 females, 12,000 males).</narrative>
  </description>
